<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy for FC Mobile Tools by TanzimFC.">
  <article class="wrap legal-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">LEGAL / PRIVACY</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-lead">Last updated: September 19, 2026</p>

    <section><h2>1. Who operates this site</h2><p>FC Mobile Tools ("FCMOBILETOOLS", "we", "us", or "our") is an independent fan project operated by TanzimFC. This policy explains how information may be processed when you visit or use our website, tools, articles, creator workspace, and related services.</p></section>

    <section><h2>2. Information you provide</h2><p>Most public tools do not require an account and are designed to work without you submitting personal information to us. We do not operate a public checkout or ask visitors to provide payment details to use the core site.</p><p>If you voluntarily contact us through an external community channel, submit information to us, or participate in the creator program, the information you choose to provide may be processed to respond, administer the relationship, review content, or operate the service.</p></section>

    <section><h2>3. Creator and private workspace data</h2><p>The private creator/admin system is separate from ordinary public browsing. Creator accounts may contain a username, display name, password credential data, profile information, website or avatar information, article drafts, revisions, review notes, publishing records, and related editorial metadata. Passwords are stored as password hashes rather than as readable passwords.</p><p>Administrative authentication also uses security session cookies. These private systems are intended for authorized personnel and contributors, not ordinary public visitors.</p></section>

    <section><h2>4. Information processed automatically</h2><p>Like most websites, our hosting and security infrastructure may process technical request information needed to deliver pages, APIs, images, and security functions. Depending on the service involved, this can include IP address, browser or device characteristics, request information, timestamps, and diagnostic information. We do not use this section to promise that a particular infrastructure provider retains or deletes logs on a specific schedule; provider-specific practices are governed by their own terms and policies.</p></section>

    <section><h2>5. Analytics</h2><p>Public pages use Google Analytics to understand aggregate website usage, including pages viewed, general traffic patterns, and technical information made available through analytics. Analytics can use cookies and similar technologies. The site is configured to provide a denied-by-default Google consent state for non-essential storage until an applicable consent signal is supplied by the configured consent solution. We use the resulting information to understand site performance and improve tools and content; it is not intended to be a public directory of individual visitors.</p></section>

    <section id="privacy-choices"><h2>6. Cookies, consent, and browser storage</h2><p>The site may use cookies and similar technologies for analytics, advertising, security, and authenticated private workspaces. Public tools and older/legacy tools can also store preferences, progress, predictions, settings, or other tool data in your browser's local storage.</p><p>Where a consent choice is required, FCMOBILETOOLS uses a site-wide privacy choice experience so the same basic privacy controls are presented consistently across the website. For Google advertising and related Google products, the consent signal may be handled through Google's Privacy &amp; messaging service and its supported consent framework. The exact choices and vendors shown to you can depend on the services active on the site at the time.</p><p>You can reopen the site's privacy choices from the <strong>Privacy Choices</strong> link in the footer when the consent service is available. You can also clear browser storage and manage cookies through your browser. See our <a href="/legal/cookie-policy">Cookie Policy</a> for more detail.</p></section>

    <section><h2>7. Third-party services</h2><p>We use or link to third-party services that help provide or support the site. These include Google Analytics, Google Fonts, Cloudflare hosting/Workers and D1 infrastructure, Cloudinary for media delivery and the private media workflow, and external platforms such as YouTube, Discord, X, and EA services. A third party may process information when your browser connects to its service or when you leave our website. Each provider's own terms and privacy practices apply to its processing.</p></section>

    <section><h2>8. Images and content delivery</h2><p>Site images may be delivered from Cloudinary or other external hosts. Public article and event content can therefore cause your browser to request an image or other resource from a third-party domain. The presence of a third-party resource does not mean that we control that provider's privacy practices.</p></section>

    <section><h2>9. How information is used</h2><p>Information may be used to operate and secure the website, authenticate authorized users, maintain creator accounts, manage editorial content, respond to requests, investigate abuse or technical problems, understand aggregate site usage, improve features, and comply with applicable obligations.</p></section>

    <section><h2>10. Data retention</h2><p>Retention depends on the type and purpose of the information. Local browser data can remain until you clear it. Creator and editorial records may be retained while an account, article, review process, or operational record is needed. Security and infrastructure records may have provider-specific retention periods. We do not promise indefinite retention or deletion on a fixed timetable unless expressly stated.</p></section>

    <section><h2>11. Security</h2><p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures appropriate to the service, including authenticated private workspaces, password hashing for creator credentials, signed sessions, and access controls. No website, cloud service, database, or transmission over the internet can be guaranteed completely secure. You should use strong, unique credentials and should not share private workspace passwords.</p></section>

    <section><h2>12. Children</h2><p>The public site is a general FC Mobile fan resource. We do not knowingly seek to collect personal information from children through the public site. If you believe personal information was submitted to us by a child and requires attention, contact us through the channels listed on the <a href="/legal/contact">Contact</a> page.</p></section>

    <section><h2>13. International processing</h2><p>Because our hosting, analytics, media, and other service providers may operate in different countries, information may be processed outside the country where you live. The safeguards and legal mechanisms applicable to a particular provider depend on that provider and the circumstances of the processing.</p></section>

    <section><h2>14. External websites</h2><p>Links to EA, YouTube, Discord, X, and other websites take you outside FCMOBILETOOLS. We do not control those services and are not responsible for their privacy practices, security, content, or availability.</p></section>

    <section><h2>15. Your choices and requests</h2><p>You may stop using the site, clear local browser data, control cookies through your browser, and decline to provide optional information. If you have a privacy-related request concerning information you directly provided to us, contact us with enough detail for us to understand the request. Any request is subject to applicable law, identity verification where reasonably necessary, and legitimate reasons we may have to retain certain records.</p></section>

    <section><h2>16. Changes to this policy</h2><p>We may revise this policy when the site, infrastructure, services, or applicable requirements change. The "Last updated" date identifies the current version. Where appropriate, material changes may also be communicated through the site or relevant community channels.</p></section>

    <section><h2>17. Contact</h2><p>For privacy questions or requests, use the official channels listed on the <a href="/legal/contact">Contact</a> page. Please do not send passwords, authentication tokens, payment details, or other unnecessary sensitive information through community messages.</p></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
